        {
          "@id": "https://www.livewelldentalva.com/services/tooth-colored-fillings#faq",
          "@type": "FAQPage",
          "isPartOf": {
            "@id": "https://www.livewelldentalva.com/services/tooth-colored-fillings#webpage"
          },
          "mainEntity": [
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "With proper care—brushing twice daily, flossing, and regular dental checkups—composite fillings typically last 7-10 years. Some patients get even longer life from their fillings, especially when placed in low-pressure areas like front teeth."
              },
              "name": "How long do tooth-colored fillings last?"
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Yes. When properly placed and bonded, composite fillings are strong enough to withstand normal chewing forces, even on back teeth. In fact, because they bond directly to your tooth structure, they actually help strengthen the remaining tooth—something amalgam fillings don't do."
              },
              "name": "Are tooth-colored fillings as strong as silver fillings?"
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Composite fillings are slightly more expensive than amalgam fillings due to the materials and technique involved. However, most dental insurance plans cover a significant portion of the cost (often 70-80%). We'll verify your benefits and provide a clear estimate before we start."
              },
              "name": "Do tooth-colored fillings cost more than silver fillings?"
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Absolutely. Many patients choose to replace visible silver fillings for aesthetic reasons or because they want to avoid mercury. Dr. Chris will evaluate your existing fillings and discuss whether replacement makes sense for your situation."
              },
              "name": "Can I replace my old silver fillings with tooth-colored ones?"
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
